nterested persons then have a period to request a hearing.\n4. **Order** granting or denying relief, issued if no hearing is requested or the request is resolved.\n\n**Rule 0-5 expedited review:** Expedited handling is requested in the filing, usually for applications substantially identical to relief the Commission already granted. The Commission decides whether to accept it, so it is not automatic.\n\n**The 45-day clock:** Rule 0-5 sets a 45-day period after filing for Commission action on the notice. It is a procedural timing marker, not a guaranteed approval date. Requests for hearing, staff comments, and amendments can extend the timeline.\n\n**Caveat:** Confirm current rule text and staff practice before relying on this, since timing varies. There is no universal total approval time.","ttft_ms":7150,"type":"result","duration_ms":8837,"uuid":"d662ef74-434c-4806-a6e8-e75cdd13f9d9","ttft_stream_ms":430,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":430,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
